abstract: >-
  Zero-dependency Node.js ESM, Python 3, and WebGL 2.0 multi-scale Artificial Life
  observatory supervising eight local endpoints across seven public repositories on
  127.0.0.1:8790. Render-only D7RO observer isolation is checked via fixed T1/T2-to-T3/T4
  coupling cells, #ifdef PICK shader preservation, and a live loopback wire-spy test
  recording every HTTP method and payload sent to a mock Asmodensius port during T1/T2
  updates. Automated example-based, live raw-socket, and seeded-random tests (14/14 Node,
  6/6 Python) cover loopback CSRF and raw-socket WebSocket Upgrade 403 CSWSH rejection,
  path-traversal containment, offline-engine DEGRADED conservation gating, 1..1,000,000
  raw-input differential Node-vs-Python clamping parity (18 adversarial cases), 112-trait
  spectral differentials, and a <=240-sample history ring; 9/9 hand-planted regression
  mutants (7 in lib/observatory_core.mjs, 2 in server.mjs) are killed. These are tests,
  not formal proofs; the repository contains 0 local Lean 4 files, has not undergone
  external peer review, and retires 0/1,900 Mega-Atlas open problems.
